.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

int bc_pty_write(bc_client_t *c, const char *data, size_t len);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes \f[B]len\f[R] bytes from \f[B]data\f[R] to the active PTY session
on the server.
The data is base64\-encoded before transmission over the wire to
preserve binary transparency (the PTY channel carries arbitrary terminal
data including control characters and escape sequences).
.PP
This function sends input to the PTY master file descriptor on the
server, which delivers it to the child process\(cqs standard input.
Common uses include sending keystrokes, command text, and terminal
control sequences (Ctrl\-C as \f[CR]\(dq\(rsx03\(dq\f[R], Ctrl\-D as
\f[CR]\(dq\(rsx04\(dq\f[R], etc.).
.PP
A PTY session must have been previously spawned with
\f[CR]bc_pty_spawn(3)\f[R].
If no PTY session is active, this function returns
\f[CR]BC_ERR_PROTOCOL\f[R].
.SH Wire protocol
Sends on \f[CR]CHAN_PTY\f[R] (channel 5):
.IP
.EX
{\(dqaction\(dq:\(dqwrite\(dq,\(dqdata\(dq:\(dqaGVsbG8gd29ybGQK\(dq}
.EE
.PP
The server decodes the base64 payload and writes the raw bytes to the
PTY master fd.
