.TE
.SH ERRORS
If the child process has already exited, the write may succeed at the
protocol level (the server accepts the frame) but the data is discarded.
The client learns of the exit through the \f[CR]bc_pty_on_exit(3)\f[R]
callback.
.PP
Large writes are sent as a single frame.
The maximum payload size is limited by \f[CR]FRAME_MAX_PAYLOAD\f[R] (1
MB) after base64 encoding, which allows approximately 750 KB of raw data
per call.
